# The folders a finished worktree may lose without a copy: build output and installed
# dependencies that a fresh checkout makes again. scripts/clean_worktrees.sh removes a merged
# worktree only when every file git does not track is inside one of these folders or has a
# byte-identical copy at the same path in the main worktree. Nothing listed means nothing is
# disposable, and a worktree holding build output is kept with the folders named. This file
# must exist for .githooks/post-merge to clean at all.
#
# One entry per line, `#` starts a comment line:
#   a NAME (build, node_modules, dist, target, .venv) matches a folder of that name anywhere,
#     except below a place that holds work (docs/build is not disposable);
#   a root-relative PATH (app/build) matches that folder only, compared folder by folder.
# Refused: an empty entry, an absolute path, "." or "..", and the places that hold work:
# .git, docs, .claude, .myagentkit, scripts. The content of these folders must also be
# git-ignored: `git worktree remove` refuses untracked files, and the worktree is then kept.
#
# One optional setting: `quiet-minutes=<n>` (default 60, at least 10). A worktree in which
# anything outside these folders, or anything in its git directory, changed less than n
# minutes ago is kept. It is a margin for a worker the process scan cannot see, not a proof.
